    "name": "consecutive-max-days-a-run-of-count-is-clean-and-the-next-date-breaks-it",
    "why": "A run of exactly count is legal and count + 1 is not, and the violation is located at THE DATE THAT BROKE THE CAP rather than at the whole run -- the only location that gives a scheduler a cell to move. p-noor holds three consecutive dates and is clean; p-ali holds four and is not. p-ali's second date carries TWO duties, which count as ONE date: a type counting duties rather than dates would break the cap a day early, on the 3rd, and would still look right on p-noor. The night on the 4th runs past midnight into the 5th and contributes its ANCHOR DATE ONLY (Decision A), so the run ends where the duties do.",
